.\" Manual page for the cajeta compiler.
.\" Generated/maintained alongside src/main.cpp printUsage; keep in sync.
.TH CAJETA 1 "2026-06-01" "cajeta" "Cajeta Compiler Manual"
.SH NAME
cajeta \- the Cajeta language compiler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cajeta
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIentry-method\fR \fIsource-root-path\fR \fIarchive-root-path\fR
.br
.B cajeta
\fIsubcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR ...]
.br
.B cajeta
.B --version
|
.B --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cajeta
compiles Cajeta source into LLVM IR, native objects/executables, or
project archives (\fB.cja\fR). The default mode emits IR; see
.B --emit
for the other output modes. The compiler links an embedded language
runtime and standard library, so a single binary is self-contained.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B archive
Archive-management surface (create / inspect / sign \fB.cja\fR archives).
.TP
.B jit\-run \fIsource-root\fR \fIpackage.Class.method\fR
Compile and run an entry point in-process via the JIT host.
.TP
.B dap
Debug Adapter Protocol server over stdio; spawned by the IDE plugin to
drive an interactive debug session.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Mode
.TP
.B --mode=debug|debug-release|release|fast|minimal
Compilation mode. Flavor aliases \fB--debug\fR, \fB--debug-release\fR,
\fB--release\fR, \fB--fast\fR, \fB--minimal\fR are also accepted.
.SS Output
.TP
.B --emit=ir|obj|cja|uber|exe
Output mode. Default \fBir\fR.
.TP
.B --classpath=\fIa.cja,b.cja\fR
Cajeta archives to ingest as dependencies (repeatable).
.TP
.B --target=\fItriple\fR
LLVM target triple. Default: host.
.TP
.B -o \fIpath\fR
Output path for the final artifact.
.SS Informational
.TP
.B --help, -h
Print the full option listing and exit.
.TP
.B --version, -V
Print version and build provenance and exit. Pair with
.B --verbose
for the LLVM and host-triple lines.
.PP
The full per-feature override and XPU option set is printed by
.BR "cajeta --help" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cajeta/
User-local toolchain root (when installed via the version manager).
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation at
.UR https://github.com/jklappenbach/cajeta
.UE .
